  "finalText": "I rebooked 7 of the 8 booking groups from ZX 440 and ZX 444. Every passenger kept their cabin, and no group was split. One group, PD9X3K, is still on ZX 440 because no connection has room for all four of them.\n\nI handled the groups in this priority order:\n\n| Booking | Passengers | Rebooked onto | Arrives JFK (9 Nov) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| WN4R8C | 1 Business, 2 Economy (from FRA) | ZX 470 to Amsterdam, then ZX 472 | 18:40 |\n| HB3K9W | 1 Business, 1 Economy (from MUC) | ZX 474 to Amsterdam, then ZX 472 | 18:40 |\n| LM2Q7H | 2 Business (from FRA) | ZX 494 to Boston, then ZX 490 | 20:25 |\n| EK1V7P | 1 Business (from MUC) | ZX 454 to London Heathrow, then ZX 462 | 21:55 |\n| PD9X3K | 4 Economy (from FRA) | Not rebooked | — |\n| OR6M2D | 3 Economy (from MUC) | ZX 454 to London Heathrow, then ZX 460 | 17:55 |\n| CB8T4F | 2 Economy (from FRA) | ZX 494 to Boston, then ZX 490 | 20:25 |\n| SV5J1N | 1 Economy (from FRA) | ZX 470 to Amsterdam, then ZX 472 | 18:40 |\n\n- **Why some groups don't get the earliest arrival:** the earliest connections had no free Business seats on the last flight, or the higher-priority groups had already taken them. That's why EK1V7P arrives later than the Economy-only groups.\n- **PD9X3K:** once the higher-priority groups were seated, every connection from Frankfurt had at most 3 free Economy seats on at least one flight.\n\nANSWER: PD9X3K",
